* ============================================================================
* workspace_memo_regression.dts - AIF-070 M2/M3: the memo-carrier proof.
*
* Proves (runtime-proven 2026-08-11 before promotion, per the
* promote-final-tests rule): a whole database posture -- 43 areas + 58
* relations -- saved INTO a memo field of the WORKSPACES catalog
* (WORKSPACE SAVE <name> MEMO) and restored FROM INSIDE THE TABLE
* (WORKSPACE LOAD <name> MEMO), then walked by both house walkers.
* One format, two carriers; the oracle byte-compare reads the token back
* from the FIELD (a len=10 truncation of the canonical 16-hex token slipped
* past a memory-ref oracle once, 2026-08-11 -- never again).
*
* Writes: WORKSPACES.dbf catalog rows (append-history, owner ruling D4; a
* rerun SUPERSEDES the prior wm_regress row -- by design, not residue).
* Requires: workspaces/cascade_all.dtschema and the cascade_erp bundle.
* Markers: WM_T1..WM_T4 must all print .T. The save line must print
* "oracle byte-compare OK" -- a transcript checkpoint, like ERP CHECK
* (a .dts marker cannot read command output; house rule).
* ============================================================================
SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

FORMULA "WORKSPACE-MEMO-PROOF-BEGIN"

* --- environment FIRST: .dtschema payloads are root-relative (measured
* 2026-08-11: a load under the wrong roots resolves 0 areas, 58 rejected) ----
SET PATH DBF SYSTEMS/CASCADE_ERP/DBF
SET PATH INDEXES SYSTEMS/CASCADE_ERP/INDEXES
SET PATH LMDB SYSTEMS/CASCADE_ERP/LMDB

* --- stand the posture up from the FILE carrier, save to the MEMO carrier ---
* The catalog self-creates on first touch (x64 flavor, planned descriptors,
* memo sidecar); the save appends an attributed, timestamped, env-stamped row.
WORKSPACE LOAD cascade_all
WORKSPACE SAVE wm_regress MEMO
WORKSPACE CLOSE

* --- restore FROM INSIDE THE TABLE ------------------------------------------
WORKSPACE LOAD wm_regress MEMO

* WM_T1: the memo-restored posture relates -- parent TOP drives the child
SELECT CASCADE_SALES_ORDERS
SET ORDER TAG SO_ID
TOP
REL REFRESH
SELECT CASCADE_SO_LINES
? "WM_T1_child_follows_parent_top:" + (SO_ID = 1)

* WM_T2: moving the parent re-drives the child (refresh-driven slaving,
* over relations that lived in a memo between save and load)
SELECT CASCADE_SALES_ORDERS
BOTTOM
REL REFRESH
SELECT CASCADE_SO_LINES
? "WM_T2_child_follows_parent_bottom:" + (SO_ID = 6)

* WM_T3: the followed child record is real data, not just a position
? "WM_T3_child_line_is_order6_line1:" + (SOLINE_ID = 11)

* --- walker #2 over the memo-restored graph ---------------------------------
SQLSEL SOLINE_ID, SO_ID FROM CASCADE_SO_Lines WHERE SO_ID = 6
* WM_T4: cursor-neutral walker agreement -- the C_T9 assertion, but over a
* posture that round-tripped through the memo carrier.
? "WM_T4_walkers_agree_over_memo_restored_graph:" + (SOLINE_ID = 11)

FORMULA "WORKSPACE-MEMO-PROOF-END"

* --- teardown: close areas, restore the x64 disk environment ----------------
WORKSPACE CLOSE
DO x64
